@startuml
' C4-PlantUML: System Context (C1) — Alternative (Central-first analytics)

' NOTE!!!
' Main idea of the alternative: much cheaper and simpler, cuz analytics & incident detection will be managed in the Central Platform
' But this may violate the requirements for working without the Internet and the speed of response to incidents
' But that might be a good alternative for the business at the MVP stage
' (cuz it will be much cheaper to miss a fight between animals when a central server is not available than buy and maintain local ML servers)

!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plantuml-stdlib/C4-PlantUML/master/C4_Context.puml

title AgroTech Farm Monitoring — System Context (C1) | Alternative: Central-first Analytics

LAYOUT_WITH_LEGEND()

' --- Actors ---
Person(farmOperator, "Farm Operator (On-duty)", "Receives alerts, monitors incidents, responds to emergencies on the farm")
Person(farmTechnician, "Farm Technician", "Maintains cameras/equipment, performs diagnostics, executes local operational tasks")
Person(sysAdmin, "System Administrator", "Manages users/roles, onboarding farms, device registration, configurations, and integrations")

' --- Our software systems ---
System_Boundary(agrotech, "AgroTech Farm Monitoring Systems") {

  System(central, "AgroTech Central Platform", "Central server platform", "Performs core video analytics & incident detection, manages farms/devices, provides UI, stores and correlates events, and sends alerts")

  System(agent, "AgroTech Farm Agent System", "Thin edge system on each farm", "Captures video streams, performs minimal preprocessing, buffers data when offline, controls equipment, and syncs raw/fragmented video + telemetry to Central when online")
}

' --- External systems / devices ---
System_Ext(cameras, "Video Cameras", "Multi-vendor cameras", "Provide live video streams from farm pens")
System_Ext(equipment, "Farm Equipment", "Feeders / Drinkers / Water filtration (multi-vendor)", "Controlled devices and sensors producing telemetry")
System_Ext(idp, "Identity Provider (SSO/OIDC)", "External auth system", "Authenticates users and issues tokens for the Central Platform")
System_Ext(notifProvider, "Notification Provider", "SMS / Push / Telephony", "Delivers notifications when Internet connectivity is available")
System_Ext(monitoring, "External Monitoring / BI System", "Metrics consumer", "Receives exported metrics for dashboards, etc")

' --- Relationships: People (mostly via Central) ---
Rel(farmOperator, central, "Monitors incidents, acknowledges alerts, views live/recorded fragments", "Web/Mobile UI")
Rel(farmTechnician, central, "Manages devices, views diagnostics, maintenance tasks", "Web UI")
Rel(sysAdmin, central, "Administers users/roles, farms onboarding, configurations", "Web UI")

' Local interaction with thin edge (limited value in this alternative)
Rel(farmTechnician, agent, "Local diagnostics & maintenance (offline)", "Local UI / LAN")

' --- Relationships: Video path (central-first) ---
Rel(cameras, agent, "Streams video", "Streaming Protocols")
Rel(agent, central, "Uploads video stream / clips + metadata for analytics", "Secure channel; high bandwidth")
Rel(central, agent, "Requests specific clips / adjusts capture policies", "Control plane")

' --- Equipment control remains at edge for offline safety ---
Rel(agent, equipment, "Controls equipment; reads telemetry", "Vendor protocols")
Rel(agent, central, "Syncs telemetry, equipment state", "Store-and-forward approach; final sync (<10 min lag)")

' --- Auth / notifications / monitoring ---
Rel(central, idp, "Authenticates users, validates tokens", "OIDC/SAML")
Rel(central, notifProvider, "Sends alerts to staff when online", "HTTPS API")
Rel(central, monitoring, "Exports metrics / KPIs", "HTTPS / Push / Batch export")

' --- Notes to highlight trade-offs (useful for ADR / review) ---
note right of central
  Central-first trade-offs:
  - Analytics & incident detection depend on connectivity
  - Network latency/throughput affect alert time
  - Higher bandwidth & storage requirements in Central
end note

note right of agent
  Thin edge agent:
  - Minimal preprocessing + buffering when offline
  - Limited/optional local heuristics only
  - Still responsible for equipment control (safety/offline)
end note

@enduml